cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the
  lineage-coupling framework it builds on (Bandler et al. 2022).
title: Undirected Clonal Coupling Network
abstract: >-
  Replicate-aware, abundance-corrected quantification of clonal coupling between
  transcriptomic states, with a within-replicate permutation null, Benjamini-
  Hochberg FDR control, and construction of a statistically filtered undirected
  lineage network.
type: software
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: Emma R. Andersson Lab
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/Emma-R-Andersson-Lab/He_et_al-Undirected-Clonal-Coupling-Network
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-12
keywords:
  - lineage tracing
  - clonal barcoding
  - single-cell RNA sequencing
  - lineage coupling
  - permutation test

# The manuscript describing the application of this software is in preparation.
# On publication, add it here as a `preferred-citation:` block and record the
# archived release DOI (for example from Zenodo) as `doi:` above, so that
# citations resolve to the paper rather than to the repository alone.

references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Single-cell delineation of lineage and genetic identity in the mouse brain
    authors:
